Bugfix: Keep a quoted local part with an '@' intact in mail addresses

Before sending, the mail layer converts the domain of every address to ASCII
(punycode). It split the address at the first '@', so a quoted local part
that itself contains one broke the address: `"a@b"@exämple.com` became
`"a@xn--b"@exmple-z2a.com`. The domain is now taken after the last '@', and
the example becomes `"a@b"@xn--exmple-cua.com`. Every other address is
converted exactly as before.
